   300	\section{Simulation, cohort and protocol}
   301	\label{sec:datasets}
   302	
   303	The implementation checks use explicit-vs-operator simulations for the PLS
   304	covariance identity and the Ridge kernel identity.  These checks verify that
   305	for fixed folds and fixed strict operators, the folded computation matches
   306	the explicit transformed computation used by an external search.
   307	
   308	The empirical benchmark uses every available AOM data run listed in the
   309	review workspace.  The regression manifest contains 61 included rows.  The
   310	main AOM-PLS comparison has 53 non-QUARTZ paired datasets for variant
   311	screening and 52 against the default-CV PLS reference.  The main
   312	AOM-Ridge comparison has 52 paired datasets against default Ridge.  Full
   313	cartesian preprocessing-HPO completed for 36 PLS datasets and 35 Ridge
   314	datasets across three seeds.  The classification cohort contains 16
   315	AOM-PLS-DA rows, with 13 paired datasets for the selected classifier.
   316	
   317	\begin{table}[t]
   318	  \centering
   319	  \caption{Cohort denominators and data-quality rules used in the main
   320	  manuscript.  Every comparison below is stated on its own paired
   321	  denominator.}
   322	  \label{tab:benchmark_diversity}
   323	  \small
   324	  \input{tables/table_benchmark_diversity.tex}
   325	\end{table}
   326	
   327	All selection steps are internal to the calibration set.  External test sets
   328	are preserved when available; otherwise deterministic SPXY or stratified
   329	splits are used \citep{kennard1969computer,galvao2005method}.  RMSEP is the
   330	primary regression metric.  Because response scales differ across traits,
   331	aggregate regression results use paired RMSEP ratios.  Classification uses
   332	balanced accuracy.  Paired tests use one-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank tests
   333	with Holm correction within the displayed family.
   334	
   335	The cartesian-HPO baselines are intentionally strong and expensive.  They
   336	enumerate 600 preprocessing combinations.  PLS-HPO uses five trials per
   337	combination; Ridge-HPO uses ten trials per combination.  These baselines were
   338	evaluated on the subset of datasets that completed within the compute budget;
   339	the LUCAS\_SOC rows did not complete, and two FUSARIUM rows failed estimator
   340	checks because the response contained NaN values.
