   131	The contributions of this work are threefold. First, we provide a large-scale evaluation of a tabular foundation model as a calibration engine for NIR chemical sensing data. Second, we quantify how preprocessing affects this model relative to established chemometric and machine-learning baselines. Third, we assess its behavior under practically important deployment conditions, including spectral outliers and extrapolation beyond the calibration domain.
