 and ASLS remain fold-local branches, not absorbed into the algebra.
 
 The study uses the full available AOM benchmark cohort: 61 regression rows in
-the manifest, 53 AOM-PLS paired datasets for variant screening, 52 paired
-AOM-Ridge datasets against Ridge, 36 completed PLS-HPO datasets, 35 completed
-Ridge-HPO datasets, and 16 classification rows.  The selected PLS variant,
+the manifest, 17 classification rows, 53 AOM-PLS paired datasets for variant
+screening, 52 paired AOM-Ridge datasets against Ridge, 36 completed PLS-HPO
+datasets, and 35 completed Ridge-HPO datasets.  Even the plain compact-bank
+AOM-PLS, fitted in a median 1.76 s, improves modestly over default PLS
+(median RMSEP ratio 0.996 on $N=52$, 32/52 wins) and reaches near-parity with
